page_texts.79:
[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-012-event-sourcing-pattern.md#traditional-approach-problems]

#### Traditional Approach (Problems)

```csharp
// Traditional state-based approach
public class TraditionalClaimService
{
    private readonly ClaimsDbContext _db;
    private readonly IAuditLogger _auditLogger;

    public async Task AdjudicateClaimAsync(Guid claimId, bool approved, decimal amount)
    {
        // Load current state
        var claim = await _db.Claims.FindAsync(claimId);

        // Update state (OVERWRITES previous state)
        var previousStatus = claim.Status;
        claim.Status = approved ? "Approved" : "Denied";
        claim.ApprovedAmount = amount;
        claim.AdjudicatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow;

        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();

        // Audit logging (SEPARATE transaction, can fail)
        try
        {
            await _auditLogger.LogAsync(new AuditEntry
            {
                EntityType = "Claim",
                EntityId = claimId,
                Action = "Adjudicated",
                OldValue = previousStatus,
                NewValue = claim.Status
                // MISSING: Why was claim approved? Which rules were evaluated?
                // MISSING: Who made the decision? What was the business reasoning?
            });
        }
        catch
        {
            // Audit logging failed - audit trail now has gap
        }
    }
}

// Problems:
// 1. Audit trail incomplete (missing business reasoning, rules evaluated)
// 2. State transitions lost (can't see Pending → Validated → Priced → Adjudicated flow)
// 3. Audit logging can fail independently from business transaction
// 4. Cannot answer "What was claim status on June 15, 2023?"
// 5. Cannot reproduce production adjudication bugs
```

page_texts.80:
[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-012-event-sourcing-pattern.md#event-sourcing-approach-solution]

#### Event Sourcing Approach (Solution)

```csharp
// Complete event history
public class EventSourcedClaimService
{
    private readonly IEventStore _eventStore;

    public async Task AdjudicateClaimAsync(AdjudicateClaimCommand command)
    {
        // 1. Load aggregate from event history
        var events = await _eventStore.LoadEventsAsync(command.ClaimId);
        var claim = Claim.LoadFromHistory(events);

        // 2. Execute command (produces events with complete context)
        claim.Adjudicate(
            approved: command.Approved,
            approvedAmount: command.ApprovedAmount,
            adjustmentReason: command.AdjustmentReason,
            rulesEvaluated: command.RulesEvaluated,
            denialReason: command.DenialReason,
            userId: command.UserId
        );

        // 3. Persist events (immutable, never fails silently)
        await _eventStore.AppendEventsAsync(
            command.ClaimId,
            claim.UncommittedEvents,
            expectedVersion: claim.Version
        );
    }
}

// Event captures complete business context
public record ClaimAdjudicatedEvent : IDomainEvent
{
    // Standard event metadata
    public Guid EventId { get; init; }
    public Guid AggregateId { get; init; }  // ClaimId
    public DateTime Timestamp { get; init; }
    public string UserId { get; init; }

    // Complete business context
    public string ClaimNumber { get; init; }
    public string AdjudicationResult { get; init; }
    public decimal BilledAmount { get; init; }
