#### Temporal Query for Retroactive Analysis

```csharp
// Query: "Was member eligible on February 15, 2024 according to eligibility
//         information available on February 20, 2024 (when claim was adjudicated)?"
var eligibilityAtAdjudicationTime = await _temporalQuery
    .GetMemberEligibilityAtTimeAsync(
        memberId: memberGuid,
        serviceDate: new DateTime(2024, 2, 15),
        asOfDate: new DateTime(2024, 2, 20)  // When claim was adjudicated
    );

// Result: Not Eligible (explains original denial)

// Query: "Is member eligible on February 15, 2024 according to CURRENT
//         eligibility information (after retroactive correction)?"
var currentEligibility = await _temporalQuery
    .GetMemberEligibilityAtTimeAsync(
        memberId: memberGuid,
        serviceDate: new DateTime(2024, 2, 15),
        asOfDate: DateTime.UtcNow  // Current eligibility knowledge
    );

// Result: Eligible (explains retroactive approval)

// This demonstrates HOW event sourcing maintains both:
// 1. Historical perspective (what we knew then)
// 2. Current perspective (what we know now)
